# Grand Abolisher bars an opponent's creature's activated abilities during your turn. Bot1 casts it on turn 1 and, on turn 3, a
# Circle of Protection: Red. Bot2's Felidar Cub (cast on turn 2 with a Plains and a Mox Pearl) has "Sacrifice this creature: Destroy
# target enchantment", no tap needed, but on Bot1's turn Bot2 can't activate it (the refusal; the Circle is a legal target, so the
# Abolisher is the only reason). Bot1's own Mox Pearl taps on its own turn, the Abolisher's controller being no opponent. On Bot2's
# turn 4 the Cub is sacrificed and the Circle destroyed.

